 The runtime injects the MUSA driver libraries, so image-build steps cannot
 import torch before a device-aware container starts. BuildKit also avoids
 resolving unrelated CUDA and ROCm base-image stages.
+
+Experimental Torch 2.2 FSDP1 import path
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+The research patch exposes the real Torch 2.2 FSDP1 APIs only when
+``RLINF_EXPERIMENTAL_FSDP1_TORCH22=1`` is set before importing RLinf. Select
+``fsdp_config.strategy=fsdp`` explicitly; requesting ``fsdp2`` fails because
+the required FSDP2 APIs are absent. Without the opt-in, Torch 2.2 remains
+unsupported by this package. The gate also recognizes vendor Torch 2.2
+prerelease version strings.
+
+This path is for a single-rank FP32 ``NO_SHARD`` strategy probe. It does not
+establish support for the official embodied Actor, model environments,
+checkpointing, offload, mixed precision, or multiple ranks. In particular,
+the existing DCP save call uses ``checkpoint_id``, which is incompatible
+with Torch 2.2's ``storage_writer`` API and is unchanged in this patch.
+
+Keep the vendor-matched Torch and Torch-MUSA pair in an isolated environment;
+the opt-in does not upgrade the driver, Toolkit, or dependencies. On MUSA,
+the probe creates an explicit MCCL default group with RLinf's configured
+collective timeout before calling the real RLinf device-mesh helper.
+The gradient-reduction helper reads the real group directly for a one-dimensional
+mesh named ``fsdp``; Torch 2.2 cannot slice that mesh. Multi-dimensional meshes
+still select the ``fsdp`` dimension explicitly.
